 "summary": "Carl Sassenrath's homoiconic messaging and scripting language built on blocks of words and some 50 literal datatypes (URLs, emails, dates, money, tuples), where domain-specific 'dialects' such as PARSE and VID are interpreted from ordinary block data; Rebol 3 was open-sourced in 2012 and continues in forks such as Ren-C.",
